WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.430
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:08.700 --> 00:12.530
What's going on? I told you to bring your girlfriend.

3
00:12.530 --> 00:16.820
I know. But I don't have a girlfriend.

4
00:16.820 --> 00:18.510
Huh?

5
00:18.510 --> 00:21.470
All I said was that I was dating someone.

6
00:21.470 --> 00:24.080
You mean...

7
00:25.850 --> 00:27.580
Nice to meet you.

8
00:27.580 --> 00:30.110
My name is Hioki. I'm Watarai's boyfriend.

9
00:30.110 --> 00:34.130
W-Wait. Are you being serious?

10
00:34.130 --> 00:35.750
Yeah.

11
00:39.500 --> 00:41.290
We even have proof.

12
00:49.710 --> 00:53.120
This makes me even more suspicious.

13
00:54.440 --> 00:56.540
Hioki, right?

14
00:56.540 --> 00:59.350
- Yeah. - Can you say his name?

15
00:59.350 --> 01:00.800
Watarai.

16
01:00.800 --> 01:03.030
His first name.

17
01:03.030 --> 01:05.670
T-Tsukasa.

18
01:06.810 --> 01:09.750
Okay, what middle school did he go to?

19
01:09.750 --> 01:11.820
Huh? I don't know.

20
01:11.820 --> 01:13.450
What club was he in in middle school?

21
01:13.450 --> 01:16.630
- I don't know. - His blood type?

22
01:16.630 --> 01:19.750
- I don't know. - His favorite food?

23
01:23.160 --> 01:25.880
You don't know anything about him.

24
01:25.880 --> 01:28.030
Sorry.

25
01:28.030 --> 01:30.150
What are you trying to pull?

26
01:30.150 --> 01:31.860
Why would you trick me?

27
01:31.860 --> 01:33.770
I'm not tricking you.

28
01:33.770 --> 01:36.210
But this is just weird.

29
01:37.460 --> 01:39.200
Weird?

30
01:40.610 --> 01:43.870
Well, I mean...

31
01:43.870 --> 01:46.950
I don't understand.

32
01:46.950 --> 01:51.040
Did you always like guys?

33
01:51.040 --> 01:54.020
Were you only dating me to blend in?

34
01:54.020 --> 01:55.940
No.

35
01:56.970 --> 01:58.880
Then why?

36
01:58.880 --> 02:01.170
Are you making fun of me?

37
02:01.170 --> 02:04.320
Because your stupid joke isn't funny.

38
02:05.980 --> 02:08.340
Stupid?

39
02:09.760 --> 02:11.870
If anything,

40
02:11.870 --> 02:14.440
you're the one making fun of us.

41
02:16.240 --> 02:18.810
You wouldn't get it, Suzu.

42
02:18.810 --> 02:19.620
Watarai.

43
02:19.620 --> 02:22.860
I worked hard to go out with Hioki.

44
02:24.410 --> 02:26.690
You know nothing about my efforts.

45
02:27.950 --> 02:29.990
You're right.

46
02:29.990 --> 02:32.400
I don't know.

47
02:32.400 --> 02:33.900
But...

48
02:34.640 --> 02:40.200
At the very least, I know more about you than him.

49
02:40.200 --> 02:41.430
What?

50
02:41.430 --> 02:42.940
I mean, it's just ridiculous.

51
02:42.940 --> 02:46.070
What sort of lover knows nothing about their partner?

52
02:50.560 --> 02:52.280
Whatever.

53
02:53.090 --> 02:57.020
If you don't believe us, fine.

54
02:57.020 --> 02:59.020
But know this.

55
02:59.020 --> 03:01.730
The only one I love is Hioki.

56
03:03.520 --> 03:05.440
Hioki, let's go.

57
03:05.440 --> 03:07.460
Huh?

58
03:07.460 --> 03:09.080
Hioki.

59
03:26.210 --> 03:28.050
I'm so sorry.

60
03:29.050 --> 03:31.260
I know that wasn't a pleasant experience...

61
03:32.630 --> 03:34.280
It's fine.

62
03:35.350 --> 03:37.460
I'm also sorry.

63
03:38.080 --> 03:40.900
Why? You did nothing wrong.

64
03:41.900 --> 03:43.980
But...

65
03:44.910 --> 03:47.800
Are you upset

66
03:47.800 --> 03:49.580
that you couldn't answer her questions?

67
03:56.850 --> 03:59.500
Don't let it bother you.

68
03:59.500 --> 04:04.680
You don't need to know the answers to her questions.

69
04:08.470 --> 04:11.080
Do you love me, Hioki?

70
04:12.720 --> 04:14.390
I do.

71
04:17.140 --> 04:19.640
Then that's plenty.

72
04:20.540 --> 04:25.710
So long as Hioki loves me, I don't need anything else.

73
04:27.670 --> 04:30.290
Come on, turn that frown upside down.

74
04:30.290 --> 04:31.750
Let's go.

75
04:39.130 --> 04:41.350
That was always my philosophy.

76
04:42.590 --> 04:44.680
But...

77
04:44.680 --> 04:46.620
Are you being serious?

78
04:46.620 --> 04:48.980
This is just weird.

79
04:58.740 --> 05:02.430
For the very first time,

80
05:02.430 --> 05:05.480
I felt like reality slapped me in the face.

81
06:07.980 --> 06:09.210
Two weeks have passed.

82
06:09.210 --> 06:12.100
[Class 3-2] [Future]

83
06:18.520 --> 06:21.520
Excuse me. Sorry.

84
06:22.470 --> 06:24.680
- No running in the halls. - Sorry.

85
06:30.570 --> 06:32.350
Watarai.

86
06:33.090 --> 06:34.360
Hioki.

87
06:34.360 --> 06:37.060
- Go, I'll catch up. - Sure.

88
06:40.450 --> 06:43.030
- You came to get me? - Yeah.

89
06:43.030 --> 06:44.400
I thought we could eat together.

90
06:44.400 --> 06:45.710
Sure.

91
06:45.710 --> 06:49.580
Oh, but I'm buying lunch from the school store today.

92
06:49.580 --> 06:52.530
I'll catch up with you and the others when I've grabbed everything.

93
06:52.530 --> 06:55.520
Can I come with you?

94
06:55.520 --> 07:00.180
- Huh? But you brought lunch. - Yeah.

95
07:00.180 --> 07:02.060
I just...

96
07:02.060 --> 07:04.310
wanted to be with you.

97
07:06.500 --> 07:10.470
Hioki's changed recently.

98
07:11.270 --> 07:13.320
Let's go.

99
07:19.340 --> 07:20.990
- Sorry to keep you. - It's fine.

100
07:20.990 --> 07:22.300
What'd you get?

101
07:22.300 --> 07:25.590
Melon bread, chocolate coronet, and yakisoba bread.

102
07:25.590 --> 07:27.370
They all sound good.

103
07:27.370 --> 07:31.470
Do you have a favorite type of bread?

104
07:31.470 --> 07:34.710
I guess melon bread, if I had to choose.

105
07:34.710 --> 07:38.420
I see. What about rice ball fillings?

106
07:40.250 --> 07:44.700
Hioki. Are you still bothered by that?

107
07:44.700 --> 07:46.280
By what?

108
07:46.280 --> 07:48.340
By what Suzu said the other day.

109
07:48.340 --> 07:51.280
No, not at all.

110
07:52.490 --> 07:54.980
He's definitely bothered by it.

111
07:54.980 --> 07:58.120
Huh. I guess Hioki can be cute after all.

112
07:58.120 --> 08:00.850
He is cute.

113
08:00.850 --> 08:04.790
He's always cute.

114
08:05.860 --> 08:07.140
Still...

115
08:07.140 --> 08:10.610
You really shouldn't let it bother you.

116
08:10.610 --> 08:13.890
But it does.

117
08:13.890 --> 08:16.200
I was completely useless.

118
08:16.200 --> 08:18.590
If anything, I only proved her point.

119
08:20.100 --> 08:24.170
So, instead, you're bashing yourself for not learning about him.

120
08:24.170 --> 08:28.330
I mean, I understand why it bothers you.

121
08:28.330 --> 08:31.660
But what's done is done.

122
08:31.660 --> 08:34.060
She's from his past. Just ignore her.

123
08:34.060 --> 08:36.050
I know I should, but...

124
08:36.050 --> 08:39.860
Watarai said he wouldn't see her again, right?

125
08:39.860 --> 08:44.300
But she might still have feelings for him.

126
08:44.300 --> 08:46.850
Does she still text Watarai?

127
08:46.850 --> 08:48.750
Well...

128
08:48.750 --> 08:50.870
I don't know.

129
08:50.870 --> 08:53.180
I blocked her.

130
08:53.180 --> 08:54.950
You blocked her?

131
08:55.740 --> 08:57.080
Yeah.

132
08:57.080 --> 08:59.540
Go, Tsukasa!

133
08:59.540 --> 09:03.670
That's an extreme measure coming from Watarai.

134
09:03.670 --> 09:05.480
He must've been seriously pissed.

135
09:05.480 --> 09:08.180
I don't think he was mad, rather...

136
09:08.180 --> 09:10.140
I was shocked.

137
09:10.970 --> 09:14.990
Honestly, I had higher hopes for her.

138
09:14.990 --> 09:17.320
Hopes?

139
09:17.320 --> 09:22.500
I thought if we talked it out, she'd accept us.

140
09:23.820 --> 09:28.290
I guess her reaction is more the norm though.

141
09:37.760 --> 09:39.840
I see.

142
09:39.840 --> 09:41.910
I don't blame you for feeling down.

143
09:41.910 --> 09:46.460
Thanks. I think Watarai isn't taking it well either.

144
09:49.210 --> 09:51.070
Then how about this?

145
09:51.070 --> 09:54.770
Let's all go let loose somewhere.

146
09:55.420 --> 09:58.580
Good idea! I'm all in!

147
09:58.580 --> 10:00.460
Let loose...

148
10:00.460 --> 10:02.360
Where?

149
10:04.870 --> 10:07.000
How about...

150
10:11.700 --> 10:13.870
Bowling?

151
10:13.870 --> 10:16.490
I haven't been in forever!

152
10:17.260 --> 10:20.980
Should we really be bowling? We have midterms coming up.

153
10:20.980 --> 10:24.530
Come on, students need a break sometimes!

154
10:24.530 --> 10:27.840
Are you good at bowling, Watarai?

155
10:27.840 --> 10:32.170
I don't know. I haven't played in a while.

156
10:32.170 --> 10:33.540
What about you, Hioki?

157
10:33.540 --> 10:34.730
I'm okay at it.

158
10:34.730 --> 10:37.240
Not great, not bad, just average.

159
10:37.240 --> 10:39.590
- I see. - So?

160
10:39.590 --> 10:41.610
Should we break up into teams?

161
10:41.610 --> 10:45.600
- Great idea. - Hold it right there!

162
10:45.600 --> 10:48.620
Allow us...

163
10:52.030 --> 10:55.060
To accept that match!

164
10:55.060 --> 10:58.060
We've been waiting for you guys!

165
11:02.960 --> 11:06.160
[Badminton Team versus Elite Four]

166
11:06.160 --> 11:07.600
Now then.

167
11:07.600 --> 11:10.190
Let's see who's the real Elite Four,

168
11:10.190 --> 11:11.810
why don't we?

169
11:11.810 --> 11:14.500
This is finally our chance!

170
11:14.500 --> 11:16.750
- I'm getting pumped! - Don't bother.

171
11:16.750 --> 11:17.870
We're definitely gonna lose.

172
11:17.870 --> 11:19.590
Enough yapping, and let's get bowling!

173
11:19.590 --> 11:21.490
Right on!

174
11:21.490 --> 11:24.170
Get your balls ready.

175
11:24.170 --> 11:27.170
I wanted to be on the same team as Hioki...

176
11:27.170 --> 11:28.800
Quit complaining.

177
11:28.800 --> 11:32.360
Yeah, we decided this fair and square with rock paper scissors.

178
11:33.040 --> 11:36.950
But he's my Hioki...

179
11:38.810 --> 11:40.530
Don't sulk.

180
11:40.530 --> 11:42.750
I know I'm yours, okay?

181
11:42.750 --> 11:46.070
Now be a good boy, and bowl with us.

182
11:46.070 --> 11:48.550
Hioki's tamed Watarai.

183
11:48.550 --> 11:52.950
Like an owner and his huge puppy.

184
11:52.950 --> 11:54.980
Hioki!

185
11:54.980 --> 11:57.880
Why're you getting it on with the hottie?

186
11:57.880 --> 12:01.540
Come watch my special form.

187
12:01.540 --> 12:03.230
Really burn it into your eyes!

188
12:03.230 --> 12:04.850
Yeah, yeah.

189
12:07.980 --> 12:10.240
Go!

190
12:12.010 --> 12:13.710
Great throw.

191
12:14.620 --> 12:15.970
[Scores]

192
12:20.280 --> 12:22.380
Go, go!

193
12:26.840 --> 12:30.190
Yeah!

194
12:31.910 --> 12:34.580
- Go ahead. - Score!

195
13:00.470 --> 13:02.740
Whenever I'm with Hioki,

196
13:02.740 --> 13:06.790
nothing else seems to matter.

197
13:06.790 --> 13:09.430
Damn it!

198
13:09.430 --> 13:10.880
Go, go...

199
13:10.880 --> 13:14.150
Yes!

200
13:14.150 --> 13:16.420
- It's fun, messing around in an arcade. - Yeah.

201
13:16.420 --> 13:19.330
It's even more fun because you're here, too.

202
13:20.770 --> 13:27.680
I stop caring about reality, what's normal, and the future.

203
13:27.680 --> 13:32.830
None of it starts to matter, when I have him.

204
13:34.260 --> 13:36.470
I'm just happy we're together.

205
13:39.730 --> 13:41.220
And I love him dearly.

206
13:41.220 --> 13:43.070
Awesome!

207
13:43.970 --> 13:45.360
You can have it.

208
13:45.360 --> 13:48.670
- You sure? - Yeah, you take it.

209
13:48.670 --> 13:51.220
- Thanks. Let's split it later. - Sure.

210
13:51.220 --> 13:53.640
I don't need anything, or anyone else.

211
13:53.640 --> 13:55.560
I only need Hioki.

212
13:56.490 --> 13:58.410
You had fun?

213
14:01.560 --> 14:03.250
But...

214
14:04.000 --> 14:05.840
Excuse me.

215
14:05.840 --> 14:07.870
I believe this is his?

216
14:07.870 --> 14:09.830
- Thank you. - Of course.

217
14:09.830 --> 14:12.200
Thanks!

218
14:14.510 --> 14:17.240
I wonder how Hioki feels?

219
14:18.920 --> 14:24.470
I might not be included in Hioki's vision of his future.

220
14:33.750 --> 14:36.960
You got this!

221
14:36.960 --> 14:38.250
Welcome back.

222
14:38.250 --> 14:40.280
Thanks.

223
14:41.410 --> 14:44.880
Say, have you guys already turned in your career forms?

224
14:44.880 --> 14:46.160
Not yet.

225
14:46.160 --> 14:49.180
I've been struggling to decide what I want to major in.

226
14:49.180 --> 14:50.770
Hotta, you're going to study agriculture, right?

227
14:50.770 --> 14:55.220
Yeah. But I haven't decided a university yet.

228
14:56.140 --> 14:57.910
I already turned mine in.

229
14:57.910 --> 14:59.040
Seriously?

230
14:59.040 --> 15:00.540
- Yeah. - A music school?

231
15:00.540 --> 15:02.840
No, a normal college.

232
15:02.840 --> 15:06.950
I like music, but realistically，

233
15:06.950 --> 15:09.620
it's hard to make a living out of it.

234
15:10.490 --> 15:12.850
I see.

235
15:12.850 --> 15:14.470
What about you, Hioki?

236
15:14.470 --> 15:16.270
Have you already chosen schools?

237
15:16.270 --> 15:17.870
Yeah, somewhat.

238
15:17.870 --> 15:19.230
Somewhere you can commute from home?

239
15:19.230 --> 15:22.060
Yeah. But I plan to try living alone.

240
15:22.060 --> 15:24.970
Huh? Alone?

241
15:24.970 --> 15:28.090
Yeah, I want to have the experience.

242
15:29.730 --> 15:32.300
I see.

243
15:32.300 --> 15:34.010
What about you, Watarai?

244
15:34.010 --> 15:34.870
Me?

245
15:34.870 --> 15:38.300
I bet he'll just attend the same school as Hioki.

246
15:38.300 --> 15:41.570
Yeah. I was going to.

247
15:41.570 --> 15:44.950
I mean, if there's nothing you want to do, that's not a bad plan.

248
15:44.950 --> 15:47.260
Something I want to do...

249
15:48.130 --> 15:50.320
They'll be flirting all around campus.

250
15:50.320 --> 15:52.470
- I can see it already. - Yeah.

251
15:52.470 --> 15:53.610
He spoke!

252
15:53.610 --> 15:55.390
We have midterms coming up.

253
15:55.390 --> 15:57.410
I wish we didn't.

254
15:57.410 --> 15:58.670
So does everyone.

255
15:58.670 --> 16:01.780
But hey, after exams, it'll be summer break!

256
16:01.780 --> 16:03.150
Should we take another trip?

257
16:03.150 --> 16:04.860
Let's have Ryoga take us!

258
16:04.860 --> 16:06.390
- We have exams. - Great idea!

259
16:06.390 --> 16:07.900
Study first.

260
16:07.900 --> 16:09.050
Please? Ask Ryoga for us!

261
16:09.050 --> 16:11.320
No thanks.

262
16:11.320 --> 16:16.330
I have no dreams. Nothing I want to be.

263
16:16.330 --> 16:18.240
I just...

264
16:19.500 --> 16:21.410
[Bookstore B&amp;B]

265
16:24.940 --> 16:26.780
Sorry.

266
16:26.780 --> 16:28.410
I have a quick errand to run.

267
16:28.410 --> 16:30.400
I'll see you guys again at school.

268
16:39.910 --> 16:44.830
[High School Math: Improving Your Score] [Books for College Entrance Exams]

269
16:44.830 --> 16:47.270
[Linkage: English Grammar]

270
16:53.070 --> 16:54.740
Watarai.

271
16:55.920 --> 16:58.600
Hioki. What's up?

272
16:58.600 --> 17:00.710
Nothing really.

273
17:00.710 --> 17:02.960
Where's everyone else?

274
17:02.960 --> 17:04.360
They headed home.

275
17:04.360 --> 17:06.900
- I see. - Yeah.

276
17:06.900 --> 17:10.690
Hioki, is there a college you're aiming for?

277
17:10.690 --> 17:13.770
Yeah, I've narrowed down my choices.

278
17:13.770 --> 17:14.820
Sort of.

279
17:14.820 --> 17:19.470
Then you have something you want to do in the future?

280
17:19.470 --> 17:21.460
Huh?

281
17:21.460 --> 17:25.650
Oh, uh... No, not really.

282
17:25.650 --> 17:29.390
I'm more focused on getting into college.

283
17:29.390 --> 17:32.670
I'll decide my major and stuff once I'm in.

284
17:32.670 --> 17:34.910
- I see. - Yeah.

285
17:38.510 --> 17:42.570
What about you? Do you have any dreams for the future?

286
17:42.570 --> 17:45.070
No dreams, but...

287
17:45.830 --> 17:48.300
I do hope for something.

288
17:48.300 --> 17:49.850
What's that?

289
17:50.710 --> 17:52.720
I just...

290
17:52.720 --> 17:56.900
I just want to be with you forever.

291
17:58.940 --> 18:01.170
I just want to live a happy life.

292
18:02.870 --> 18:04.250
A happy life.

293
18:04.250 --> 18:05.560
Yeah.

294
18:05.560 --> 18:07.450
What does that entail?

295
18:07.450 --> 18:08.980
Huh?

296
18:09.780 --> 18:12.100
Let's see...

297
18:12.830 --> 18:14.360
[Fine Home]

298
18:18.840 --> 18:22.100
It means I'd try living in a place like this.

299
18:23.340 --> 18:25.460
Rent would be expensive.

300
18:25.460 --> 18:27.470
Yeah, fair point.

301
18:27.470 --> 18:30.680
What about you? Where would you want to live?

302
18:30.680 --> 18:32.360
- Me? - Yeah.

303
18:32.360 --> 18:33.650
Does it have to be a realistic option?

304
18:33.650 --> 18:36.150
Not at all. Dreaming big costs nothing.

305
18:36.150 --> 18:37.850
I guess so.

306
18:43.440 --> 18:45.000
Then how's this?

307
18:45.000 --> 18:46.710
A penthouse suite?

308
18:46.710 --> 18:49.140
It doesn't have to be a penthouse.

309
18:49.140 --> 18:51.590
But I'd like a nice view.

310
18:51.590 --> 18:53.270
What else do you want?

311
18:54.890 --> 18:57.530
Plenty of storage space.

312
19:00.500 --> 19:01.850
This much would do.

313
19:01.850 --> 19:04.210
That's a huge closet.

314
19:04.880 --> 19:08.360
Yeah. I don't own that much clothes,

315
19:08.360 --> 19:11.180
but we need to account for yours, right?

316
19:13.230 --> 19:14.680
Huh?

317
19:17.920 --> 19:20.210
Wait, you...

318
19:20.210 --> 19:22.740
Sorry, do you not actually have that much?

319
19:22.740 --> 19:25.450
No, I mean...

320
19:25.450 --> 19:28.350
This whole time we've been talking houses,

321
19:28.350 --> 19:31.560
it was with the intent of living together?

322
19:33.190 --> 19:35.370
Was it not?

323
19:35.370 --> 19:39.340
Huh? But you said you wanted to live alone...

324
19:39.340 --> 19:44.280
While I'm a student, yeah.

325
19:46.980 --> 19:51.620
Then after we graduate college,

326
19:51.620 --> 19:55.040
you wouldn't mind living with me?

327
19:55.750 --> 19:58.280
Yeah. But if you'd rather not...

328
19:58.280 --> 20:00.090
No, I'd love to!

329
20:02.720 --> 20:06.820
I... I've never been as happy as I am now.

330
20:08.860 --> 20:11.180
- Ever? - Ever.

331
20:15.270 --> 20:19.560
Still, if we wanted to live it big,

332
20:19.560 --> 20:22.300
we'd have to earn a crazy salary.

333
20:22.300 --> 20:24.450
Don't worry.

334
20:24.450 --> 20:27.750
I'll earn enough for the both of us.

335
20:28.990 --> 20:30.480
Huh?

336
20:31.350 --> 20:35.420
I'll give you everything you could ever want.

337
20:37.010 --> 20:38.770
Thanks.

338
20:38.770 --> 20:39.900
I'll look forward to that.

339
20:39.900 --> 20:42.710
Yeah. You better.

340
20:44.920 --> 20:47.210
I was joking.

341
20:47.210 --> 20:49.690
- Well, I wasn't. - Huh?

342
20:52.580 --> 20:57.300
So... were you being serious?

343
20:57.300 --> 20:59.280
Huh? No, I was joking.

344
20:59.280 --> 21:01.510
Not about that.

345
21:01.510 --> 21:04.630
About living together one day.

346
21:04.630 --> 21:07.970
Oh, that. Yeah, I'd be down.

347
21:07.970 --> 21:10.110
Promise?

348
21:10.110 --> 21:11.600
Yeah.

349
21:11.600 --> 21:13.830
Pinky promise.

350
21:18.530 --> 21:20.470
Thank you, Hioki.

351
21:20.470 --> 21:24.820
Now I know what to do.

352
21:24.820 --> 21:26.280
You make it sound like I helped.

353
21:26.280 --> 21:27.960
You did.

354
21:27.960 --> 21:30.570
I mean it.

355
21:30.570 --> 21:32.260
Thank you.

356
21:33.540 --> 21:37.910
I'm no longer unsure of myself.

357
21:41.670 --> 21:43.550
Should we get going?

358
21:43.550 --> 21:44.970
Yeah.

359
22:05.870 --> 22:10.380
So long as I'm in Hioki's future,

360
22:10.380 --> 22:13.110
then all I need to do now is press on.

361
22:17.500 --> 22:22.900
[Fine Home]

362
22:26.140 --> 22:28.460
[Meio University]

363
22:35.040 --> 22:39.350
If it's for Hioki's sake,

364
22:41.600 --> 22:45.930
I'll make any dream a reality.

365
22:56.070 --> 22:58.280
We're here! [Final summer vacation of high school]

366
22:58.280 --> 23:00.640
What should we do now?

367
23:00.640 --> 23:01.890
Say cheese!

368
23:01.890 --> 23:04.990
I'm so in love with you, it's a problem.

369
23:04.990 --> 23:06.980
Well, I love you more.

370
23:06.980 --> 23:10.910
Hioki, there's something I need to tell you.

371
23:10.910 --> 23:14.200
- A bug! A bug! - A bug?
